<mxCell id="n47" value="VERIFICATION NOTE (acknowledged in code). The entire WhatsApp Flows path — Flow JSON validity, the encryption round-trip with real Meta, INIT vs data_exchange action handling — cannot be exercised without a Meta Business Account. Unit tests cover the crypto round-trip + an IV-flip known-answer vector, but nothing end-to-end. All flow ids / keys are empty in the repo. This is inherent, not a defect — but it means every Flow-based step is ASSUMED, not verified." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="700" width="420" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e48" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=0;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="n47"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n49" value="STRENGTH. Outbox is genuinely durable: startup sweep + periodic sweep + immediate enqueue all converge on a SKIP LOCKED claim, correct under restart and concurrency. Signature check + inbound dedup by wa_message_id present." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1120" y="700" width="360" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e50" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n39" target="n49"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
